1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,700
Football Intelligence Platform — Near-live, evidence-grounded match intelligence

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,360
This idea started when I studied the needs of an amateur football club.

3
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,373
The club could record a match,

4
00:00:10,373 --> 00:00:14,733
but information that might influence football decisions was often unavailable during the game,

5
00:00:14,733 --> 00:00:15,740
delivered too late,

6
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:18,759
or difficult to trust without checking the video again.

7
00:00:18,759 --> 00:00:28,150
I wanted to start at amateur level because clubs with the least money should still have access to the standard of evidence normally associated with top professional football.

8
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:31,840
Coaches need more than footage. They need evidence they can use.

9
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:32,940
Completed passes, possession,

10
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:38,076
turnovers and shots on target matter most while the match can still be changed.

11
00:00:38,076 --> 00:00:42,111
During play, an authorised screen can show the relevant match statistics,

12
00:00:42,111 --> 00:00:44,679
including possession and zone performance. At half-time,

13
00:00:44,679 --> 00:00:52,015
the same evidence expands into a dressing-room view with the deeper zone and match statistics a coach needs for discussion.

14
00:00:52,015 --> 00:00:56,050
The system informs the decision; the coach decides what must change.

15
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:59,670
The opportunity is not simply another camera or another dashboard.

16
00:00:59,670 --> 00:01:03,651
It is one traceable flow from the match to useful evidence:

17
00:01:03,651 --> 00:01:06,909
capture the whole pitch, understand the state of play,

18
00:01:06,909 --> 00:01:08,357
calculate agreed football events,

19
00:01:08,357 --> 00:01:11,615
and deliver the resulting statistics while they still matter.

20
00:01:11,615 --> 00:01:18,130
Every published number must remain connected to the video evidence and the exact rules-engine version that produced it.

21
00:01:18,130 --> 00:01:22,623
Here is the proposed architecture. One elevated panoramic main camera,

22
00:01:22,623 --> 00:01:25,768
positioned on the long side near halfway,

23
00:01:25,768 --> 00:01:30,261
continuously preserves the full-pitch geometry, team spacing and off-ball movement.

24
00:01:30,261 --> 00:01:36,552
The blue and red player shapes show how the calibrated view supports tactical context.

25
00:01:36,552 --> 00:01:39,247
Green arrows connect completed passing lanes.

26
00:01:39,247 --> 00:01:43,291
The dashed amber lane shows where possession is lost.

27
00:01:43,291 --> 00:01:46,436
A second opposing panoramic camera is recommended,

28
00:01:46,436 --> 00:01:50,480
while two goal-end cameras remain optional when budget permits.

29
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:53,399
The purple lines are infrastructure, not passes.

30
00:01:53,399 --> 00:02:05,074
Wired Cat six and Power over Ethernet feeds run around the pitch perimeter into a network switch and a locked high-speed GPU workstation in the clubhouse security office.

31
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:07,576
Video and analysis remain locally controlled,

32
00:02:07,576 --> 00:02:10,078
with BitLocker-encrypted storage and authorised access.

33
00:02:10,078 --> 00:02:17,584
The platform is designed to deliver near-live match intelligence in rolling one-minute updates using secure local GPU processing.

34
00:02:17,584 --> 00:02:18,835
For the pilot,

35
00:02:18,835 --> 00:02:24,672
every sixty-second window must be processed and published before the next window is due,

36
00:02:24,672 --> 00:02:27,591
while maintaining the agreed per-statistic accuracy target.

37
00:02:27,591 --> 00:02:32,178
Stateful overlapping work carries possession, match state and unresolved events forward,

38
00:02:32,178 --> 00:02:34,680
suppresses duplicates, and updates cumulative totals.

39
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:39,050
The match-day screens show statistics, not automatic tactical instructions. During play,

40
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:45,009
the coach can see the current match totals together with useful possession and zone indicators.

41
00:02:45,009 --> 00:02:48,585
At half-time, the dressing-room view expands those same numbers:

42
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:52,558
possession won and lost by zone, completed passes, turnovers, shots,

43
00:02:52,558 --> 00:02:54,544
final-third entries and recent trends.

44
00:02:54,544 --> 00:03:02,490
The coaching team combines that evidence with what it has observed to conduct the match discussion and decide the response.

45
00:03:02,490 --> 00:03:06,295
The current Review application is the continuous validation environment,

46
00:03:06,295 --> 00:03:09,677
not the match-day dashboard. Across controlled video segments,

47
00:03:09,677 --> 00:03:12,213
authorised human validators inspect the evidence.

48
00:03:12,213 --> 00:03:15,173
Copilot assists with football-law and analytics knowledge,

49
00:03:15,173 --> 00:03:18,555
but it does not approve its own proposal.

50
00:03:18,555 --> 00:03:22,360
Each independent review is compared with the rules-engine result.

51
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:26,587
A supported disagreement may improve only a general football rule,

52
00:03:26,587 --> 00:03:29,124
never one timestamp or manual label.

53
00:03:29,124 --> 00:03:33,351
Protected regressions then check that previously accepted behaviour still holds.

54
00:03:33,351 --> 00:03:39,270
The validated rules-engine version is what the local GPU runs against new match footage.

55
00:03:39,270 --> 00:03:40,908
For an amateur club,

56
00:03:40,908 --> 00:03:45,413
the target installed core is below twelve thousand euros before tax:

57
00:03:45,413 --> 00:03:49,917
one panoramic main camera, secure local GPU processing, storage, networking, installation,

58
00:03:49,917 --> 00:03:53,603
calibration and initial support. It is a planning target,

59
00:03:53,603 --> 00:03:57,288
not a quotation, and each site must be assessed.

60
00:03:57,288 --> 00:04:01,793
The core does not require mandatory cloud processing or cloud storage.

61
00:04:01,793 --> 00:04:06,297
Lower-cost camera platforms often add recurring subscriptions, while professional video, data,

62
00:04:06,297 --> 00:04:14,078
cloud and analyst services are commonly sold as bespoke packages and can collectively reach thousands of euros per month.

63
00:04:14,078 --> 00:04:19,401
That is why the fair comparison is the complete three-year cost of ownership,

64
00:04:19,401 --> 00:04:21,039
not one headline subscription.

65
00:04:21,039 --> 00:04:28,410
A second panoramic camera and goal-end views remain optional upgrades rather than costs every amateur club must carry.

66
00:04:28,410 --> 00:04:33,240
Today, the working proof is offline: calibrated footage, tracking, football state,

67
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:37,630
event review and regression-protected output. Live ingest, professional multi-camera operation,

68
00:04:37,630 --> 00:04:41,582
stadium deployment and durable player identity are next-stage capabilities,

69
00:04:41,582 --> 00:04:42,899
not completed claims.

70
00:04:42,899 --> 00:04:52,998
Our future Query By Probability concept keeps the main camera continuous and queries only the relevant secondary view for a short low-confidence moment.

71
00:04:52,998 --> 00:04:58,706
The controlled pilot target is at least ninety-five percent against independently reviewed references,

72
00:04:58,706 --> 00:05:01,340
reported separately for each agreed statistic.

73
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:06,043
We propose a staged co-development pilot between a professional football club and Xebia:

74
00:05:06,043 --> 00:05:09,660
define the statistics that matter, agree accuracy and latency targets,

75
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:11,107
validate on controlled matches,

76
00:05:11,107 --> 00:05:15,086
and build a credible route from grassroots affordability to professional performance.

77
00:05:15,086 --> 00:05:19,066
The goal is not more data after the moment has passed.

78
00:05:19,066 --> 00:05:24,130
It is trusted football intelligence while the next decision can still change the match.

79
00:05:24,430 --> 00:05:29,830
Professional Football + Xebia — A staged co-development pilot

